# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props interface: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to verify

1. Run `yarn test:code` (ESLint) and `yarn test:typecheck` (`tsc`) from the repo root after substantive edits.
2. For new components, confirm a colocated `*.test.tsx` exists or existing tests were updated.
3. Quick review: named exports only, `ComponentNameProps` naming, kebab-case vs PascalCase file names match the rules above.
